-- INDEPENDENT TEST PASS for Magna Carta (1297). Expected values are from ANSWERS.md (written before any .l4 file was opened).
-- Scenario numbers below are the numbers in ANSWERS.md.
-- Mapping of my vocabulary to the encoding's: TRUE for "breach/forbidden" = `forbidden by chapter 29` / `forbidden by the text`;
-- FALSE for "not a breach" = `not forbidden by chapter 29`; NOT COVERED = the encoding's own `not covered by ...` constructor.
-- Four assertions (156, 159, 172, 178) failed on the first run: the author expected FALSE ("the text says no") and the first version of the
-- encoding answered "not covered". The author wrote each as NOT (answer EQUALS `not covered ...`) and left it failing. On 2026-10-30 they were
-- restated, each with a -- RECONCILED comment that quotes the original; 178 is an encoder repair, the other three follow the encoding (see NOTES.md).
-- Lines 48 and 76 are string carriers (a list of Acts, a list of titles): there I check that the item is absent; they cannot tell silent
-- from no, and I expected NOT COVERED, so absence is consistent with my answer (TYPE-LIMIT in the comment marks them; not a finding).
-- Lines marked PROXY use the closest function, which asks a neighbouring question.
-- Scenarios the encoding has no function for are NOT asserted here; they are the -- GAP lines at the end of this file.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers (mine; they read the encoding's strings and lists, they restate nothing of the law)

GIVEN needle IS A STRING
      haystack IS A STRING
      start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my infix scan` needle haystack start MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF start PLUS (STRINGLENGTH needle) GREATER THAN (STRINGLENGTH haystack) THEN FALSE
        IF (SUBSTRING haystack start (STRINGLENGTH needle)) EQUALS needle THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `my infix scan` needle haystack (start PLUS 1)

GIVEN needle IS A STRING
      haystack IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my text has` needle haystack MEANS `my infix scan` needle haystack 0

GIVEN items IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`my joined` items MEANS
    CONSIDER items
        WHEN EMPTY THEN ""
        WHEN item FOLLOWED BY rest THEN item APPEND (" | " APPEND (`my joined` rest))

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`my status of` n MEANS
    CONSIDER `the status shown for chapter` n
        WHEN `shown repealed` entry THEN "repealed"
        WHEN `shown repealed in part` entry THEN "repealed in part"
        WHEN `no repeal annotation shown` THEN "no annotation"
        WHEN `outside the cc. 1-37 the extract names` THEN "outside"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`my entry for` n MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry among` `the chapters that have a repeal status entry` `and` `the repeal status entries` `for chapter` n
        WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
        WHEN JUST e THEN e

GIVEN label IS A STRING
      lo IS A NUMBER
      hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my count of chapters with status` label lo hi MEANS
    IF lo GREATER THAN hi
    THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `my status of` lo EQUALS label THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (`my count of chapters with status` label (lo PLUS 1) hi)

GIVEN needle IS A STRING
      lo IS A NUMBER
      hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my count of entries having` needle lo hi MEANS
    IF lo GREATER THAN hi
    THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `my text has` needle (`my entry for` lo) THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (`my count of entries having` needle (lo PLUS 1) hi)

GIVEN passage IS A Passage
GIVETH A STRING
`my titles at` passage MEANS
    CONSIDER `the speaker named at the head of` passage
        WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
        WHEN JUST s THEN `my joined` (titles OF s)

